# DHF-REQ: keel/requirement-123
#
# raw/filesystem.cyclonedx.json is generated, not committed.
#
# syft records the absolute path of every component it catalogued, so the file
# states the directory of the checkout that produced it. Committing it makes the
# SBOM non-convergent: a refresh from a different worktree rewrites those paths
# with no inventory change, and a 545 KB artifact that always churns stops being
# read — which is how a real inventory change passes unexamined (keel/issue-149).
#
# Nothing downstream reads the committed copy. grype re-scans a freshly generated
# one, and linked-components.md / cve.md are what review consumes. The two CVE
# artifacts beside it carry no host paths and stay tracked.
raw/filesystem.cyclonedx.json
